  "title": "Guan Bunga",
  "description": "Mangal Singhku, a Ho speaker, describes Guan Bunga, a ceremony of the Ho community of India. Guan Bunga means \"cattle pen worship\", and the head of the family, the desauli, performs it. Subhashish Panigrahi recorded it at Keshpada, Mayurbhanj district, Odisha, India, for his 2019 documentary Mage Porob. Panigrahi edited several videos that were unused or little used in the film into one short documentary, published under the 𑢼𑣃𑣃𑣊 𑢾𑣁𑣌𑣁𑣖 (Ruum Sakam) project in 2024. Ho subtitles are by Ganesh Birua, the Odia translation is by Panigrahi, and the English translation is by Birua and Panigrahi, edited by Panigrahi.",
